---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../../components/Hero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Advertising companies in our apps | Ludiven Studio"
	description="Who receives what when you accept personalised advertising in Pétanque Scan, Pétanque Meet, Pétanque Game and Dragon Gems."
	lang="en"
	alternates={{ fr: '/publicite/societes/', en: '/en/publicite/societes/', es: '/es/publicite/societes/', de: '/de/publicite/societes/', it: '/it/publicite/societes/' }}
>
	<div class="wrapper stack gap-12 legal">
		<Hero
			title="Advertising companies"
			tagline="Who receives what when you accept personalised advertising in our apps."
		/>

		<p class="updated">This is the page behind the “See the companies” link in the consent window of our apps: Pétanque Scan, Pétanque Meet, Pétanque Game and Dragon Gems. Last updated: 27 November 2026.</p>
		<p class="updated">This is a courtesy translation. In case of discrepancy, the <a href="/publicite/societes/" hreflang="fr">original French version</a> prevails.</p>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>1. What you accept</h2>
			<p>One thing only, <strong>personalised advertising</strong>: choosing ads based on your profile, limiting how often they repeat, measuring how well they work and fighting fraud.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>2. Who serves it</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Unity Ads</strong> and <strong>ironSource Ads</strong>, through <strong>Unity LevelPlay</strong>: Unity Technologies and its subsidiary ironSource.</li>
				<li>
					Through their auctions, the ad request may go, with personal data such as your phone's advertising identifier, to <strong>other advertising companies</strong>. Unity publishes their list, about 95 companies, in section 13 of its
					<a href="https://unity.com/legal/game-player-and-app-user-privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy policy</a>.
				</li>
				<li><strong>Google AdMob</strong> (Google Ireland Limited), in Pétanque Game since its version 1.0.20, through Unity LevelPlay's bidding; on iPhone, only outside the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom and Switzerland. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from partner apps</a>.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>In Pétanque Game, since version 1.0.20:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>On iPhone</strong>, the only question is Apple's, the tracking permission. If you allow it, an information note is shown, then the companies above serve ads. If you refuse it, or if it is restricted on your iPhone, none of these companies starts and no other window opens: the game only shows our own videos.</li>
				<li><strong>On Android</strong>, the question is asked by Google's consent form (Google User Messaging Platform), which shows the companies and their purposes itself. Where Google asks nothing, our own window asks it, and this page is its “See the companies” link.</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>3. If you refuse</h2>
			<p>The advertising module does not start: nothing is sent to these companies. The app only shows our own ads, for our other apps, whose list is read from this website. In Pétanque Game on Android, Google's form contacts Google at each launch to show itself, before your answer.</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>4. On iPhone</h2>
			<p>If you refuse the tracking Apple asks about, ads are not personalised and our partners do not receive your iPhone's advertising identifier, even if you accepted advertising. In Pétanque Game, since version 1.0.20, this refusal starts none of these companies (see above).</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>5. Changing your mind</h2>
			<p>At any time, in the app's settings. Withdrawing stops personalised advertising and is passed on to the advertising module. The app asks for your choice again after 6 months. In Pétanque Game, since version 1.0.20: on iPhone (iOS 14 or later), in Settings › Privacy &amp; Security › Tracking, by turning Pétanque Game on or off; in the game, the "Ad choices" line only exists after a yes and points to these Settings. On Android and on an older iPhone, in Options › "Ad choices" (on Android, Google's form or our window).</p>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-2">
			<h2>6. For each app</h2>
			<p>The details of the data and of your rights are in each app's privacy policy:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><a href="/en/petanque-scanner/confidentialite/">Pétanque Scan</a></li>
				<li><a href="/en/petanque-meet/confidentialite/">Pétanque Meet</a></li>
				<li><a href="/en/petanque-game/confidentialite/">Pétanque Game</a></li>
				<li><a href="/en/dragons-gems/confidentialite/">Dragon Gems</a></li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
